From 0f5976982a2ea76c23d499dad8327cb5e46fb63d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 18:59:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(hosted): skip discarded discovery for empty canonical
 owners [daveey]

Root (happened): bindings freshly reads the indexed canonical owner set but
always discovers rooms, even when no binding can survive the empty-set filter.
Root (not caught): selector tests verified output and indexed work, not absence
of superclass/list_rooms calls. Earlier PR3352 intentionally left this cost.
Recurrence: distinct residual work after merged schema/selector optimizations,
not a regression of them. No schema, caching, polling or authority changes.

Return () only after the successful fresh owner read closes. Keep nonempty
superclass behavior verbatim. Independent pre-implementation semantic review
approved: constructor/import retain initialization and supervisor maintenance
remains outside discovery. Incidental superclass errors are intentionally not
observed when there are no eligible owners; owner read errors still propagate.

Proof: 8 new regression cases; RED 4 failures, GREEN all 8 pass; removing the
return kills 4 cases. Existing 6 indexed selector tests unchanged and pass.
All 116 direct service/driver consumer files: 931 passed, 0 failed on Linux
(one file has macOS platform skips). scripts/check: 20 checks, ok.

Pool thread-CPU A/B, 1k/20k/100k unrelated metadata, 3 fixtures/arm, 15 trials:
empty complete bindings 1.407/1.516/1.530 ms -> .00684/.00712/.00718 ms;
actual empty supervisor cycle+maintenance 1.696/1.624/1.619 ms ->
.0330/.0378/.0370 ms. Real synchronous nonempty full cycles including room
work/maintenance are noisy (-0.59% to +0.35% improvement), not a speedup claim.
540 raw records include 90 warmups. No DB/superclass mocks in benchmarks.
This does not establish live mini CPU acceptance; origin t_0f4ba25fadea4b66
owns normal deployment and >=600s idle/hosted follow-up measurements.
